# Story: somebody who knows nine keys wants the rest. They press ⌃⌥G and type what the thing is called in the menu: a few letters, Return.
# It acts on the window they were in, is answered on screen as a key is, and one undo takes it back. Before they type, Go to… lists
# places as ever; whoever types a piece of a window's name still goes to the window; and `find <text>`, which shows nothing, goes to
# places and runs nothing.
# Reference: board 0.14 (IDEAS I22, QUESTIONS Q29, 1); docs/features/F27-window-finder.md, "Commands". Window ids start at 101.
open Safari
open Notes
open Mail
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
focus 103
expect floating 103
# "Dock Focused Window ▸ Left": Mail had the keyboard when the palette opened.
find
expect ok
finder-type dock left
finder-choose
expect docked 103
expect left-of 103 101
# "Adjust ▸ Balance Sizes" by three letters, after Mail was made wider.
expect size 103 345x851
grow
grow
find
finder-type bal
finder-choose
expect size 103 345x851
expect size 101 345x851
# "Undo…", whatever it is called just now: the balancing, the growing, the dock.
find
finder-type undo
finder-choose
find
finder-type undo
finder-choose
expect docked 103
expect size 103 345x851
find
finder-type undo
finder-choose
expect floating 103
expect docked 101
# "Float All Windows", one of the ways back.
find
finder-type float all
finder-choose
expect floating 101
expect floating 102
# What the menu greys out is listed, says "not now", and runs nothing: the palette says so and stays.
flush
find
finder-type step out
finder-choose
expect silent
finder-cancel
# Letters that stand together in a window's name are that window, though a command's word begins with them.
open Preview
find
finder-type vie
finder-choose
expect focused 104
# A window still comes first where it is the better match, and Return goes there.
dock 101 left
find
finder-type saf
finder-choose
expect focused 101
# Without the palette nothing is run: a script or a link that says `find` means a place.
find float all
expect fail
expect docked 101
find pause
expect fail
